# promise: #692
# Settings ▸ Tabs "Edit the address in the sidebar" (#344): a click on the sidebar's empty space ends
# the edit and puts the address back, with the sidebar shown and with the hidden sidebar slid out at
# the window's edge, which stays out while its address is edited. Until 0.1.54 only a click on the
# page ended it: a click in the sidebar's own window never moved the keys from the field.
budget rss=800 stalls50=20
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": false, "editAddressInPlace": true}
cra://debug?windowSize=1200x800
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=edit
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 2
cra://debug?urlFieldEdit=click
expect-log url field click: editing .*n=edit, command bar closed
cra://debug?clickAt=120,600
wait 1
cra://debug?urlFieldEdit=state
expect-log url field state: not editing, command bar closed

# The hidden sidebar, out at the edge.
cra://action/toggleSidebar
wait 1
cra://debug?floatingSidebar=hold
wait 1
cra://debug?urlFieldEdit=click
expect-log url field click: editing .*n=edit, command bar closed
cra://debug?floatingSidebar=release
cra://debug?floatingSidebar=pointerAway
wait 1
cra://debug?floatingSidebar=state:editing
expect-log floating sidebar editing: out$
cra://debug?clickAt=120,600&target=floating
wait 1
cra://debug?urlFieldEdit=state
expect-log url field state: not editing, command bar closed
